       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks wrong.\n\n**Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is 5 times the maximum dose.** For adults, amlodipine is usually started at 2.5\u20135 mg once daily, and the most anyone should get is 10 mg once daily. A 50 mg dose could cause severe low blood pressure and shock, and dialysis doesn't remove amlodipine well, so an overdose is hard to reverse.\n\nThis might be a typo for **5 mg**, which is a common starting dose for an adult with normal kidney and liver function. Can you tell me which dose you want?\n\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, or\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, or\n- another dose, with the clinical reason if it's above 10 mg.\n\nI'll enter the order as soon as you confirm."
