       "text": "I won't enter amlodipine 50 mg daily, even with your confirmation. I can't find any clinical setting where 50 mg is an appropriate dose:\n\n- **The highest labeled dose is 10 mg once daily.** Going above that doesn't lower blood pressure much more, but it does cause more swelling and low blood pressure.\n- **50 mg falls in the overdose range.** Amlodipine overdoses cause long-lasting low blood pressure that is hard to treat. Because the drug's half-life is 30\u201350 hours, the effects would build up with each daily dose.\n- **You haven't given a reason for the higher dose,** and 50 mg is exactly what you'd get by typing \"5\" with an extra zero.\n\n**Options:**\n\n1. **If you meant 5 mg or 10 mg,** tell me which and I'll enter it right away.\n2. **If you really do intend 50 mg** for a reason I'm not aware of, please discuss it with the clinical pharmacist. Then enter it yourself with documented approval and the reason, so it goes through pharmacy verification.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
